      {
        id: "n2",
        role: "assistant",
        text: "Yes. A partial index on (user_id, created_at) WHERE read_at IS NULL stays small because most notifications are read within a day. Postgres only uses it when the query repeats the same predicate, so keep read_at IS NULL in the WHERE clause.",
